{"entryType": "UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)", "primaryAccession": "O43315", "secondaryAccessions": ["Q9NP32"], "uniProtkbId": "AQP9_HUMAN", "entryAudit": {"firstPublicDate": "1998-12-15", "lastAnnotationUpdateDate": "2026-06-10", "lastSequenceUpdateDate": "2011-01-11", "entryVersion": 199, "sequenceVersion": 2}, "annotationScore": 5.0, "organism": {"scientificName": "Homo sapiens", "commonName": "Human", "taxonId": 9606, "lineage": ["Eukaryota", "Metazoa", "Chordata", "Craniata", "Vertebrata", "Euteleostomi", "Mammalia", "Eutheria", "Euarchontoglires", "Primates", "Haplorrhini", "Catarrhini", "Hominidae", "Homo"]}, "proteinExistence": "1: Evidence at protein level", "proteinDescription": {"recommendedName": {"fullName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000303", "source": "PubMed", "id": "10564231"}], "value": "Aquaporin-9"}, "shortNames": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305", "source": "PubMed", "id": "10564231"}], "value": "AQP-9"}]}, "alternativeNames": [{"fullName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305", "source": "PubMed", "id": "30420639"}], "value": "Aquaglyceroporin-9"}}, {"fullName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000312", "source": "EMBL", "id": "AAF16677.1"}], "value": "Small solute channel 1"}}]}, "genes": [{"geneName": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000312", "source": "HGNC", "id": "HGNC:643"}], "value": "AQP9"}, "synonyms": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000312", "source": "EMBL", "id": "AAF16677.1"}], "value": "SSC1"}]}], "comments": [{"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "P56627"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000250", "source": "UniProtKB", "id": "Q9JJJ3"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "10564231"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "26837049"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "30420639"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "35054513"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9514918"}], "value": "Aquaglyceroporins form homotetrameric transmembrane channels, with each monomer independently mediating glycerol and water transport across the plasma membrane along their osmotic gradient (PubMed:10564231, PubMed:30420639, PubMed:35054513, PubMed:9514918). AQP9 is the primary route for glycerol uptake in hepatocytes, supporting hepatic gluconeogenesis (By similarity). It exhibits broad specificity and may transport various small, non-charged solutes, including carbamides, polyols, purines, and pyrimidines (PubMed:10564231). AQP9 may also facilitate hepatic urea extrusion (PubMed:10564231, PubMed:9514918). Due to its permeability to lactate, AQP9 might participate in the astrocyte-to-neuron lactate shuttle, supplying neurons with energy (PubMed:10564231, PubMed:35054513). Additionally, AQP9 is permeable to arsenite, contributing to arsenic excretion by the liver and providing partial protection against arsenic toxicity (PubMed:10564231). It is also permeable to H2O2 in vivo (PubMed:26837049). Could also be permeable to ammonium (By similarity)"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION"}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "glycerol(in) = glycerol(out)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:29675"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:17754"}], "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "10564231"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "30420639"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "35054513"}]}}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "H2O(in) = H2O(out)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:29667"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:15377"}], "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "30420639"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269", "source": "PubMed", "id": "9514918"}]}}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "ur